  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"48\" data-end=\"69\">Direct Renin test</strong> measures the concentration of <strong data-start=\"100\" data-end=\"116\">active renin</strong> in the blood and is primarily used to evaluate disorders of <strong data-start=\"177\" data-end=\"206\">blood pressure regulation</strong>, <strong data-start=\"208\" data-end=\"226\">sodium balance</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"232\" data-end=\"258\">aldosterone production</strong>. It is often interpreted alongside <strong data-start=\"294\" data-end=\"309\">aldosterone</strong> to calculate the <strong data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"363\">aldosterone-to-renin ratio (ARR)</strong>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Renin Level</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Possible Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Low</strong></td>\n<td>Suggests <strong>suppressed renin</strong> secretion &ndash; often due to: - <strong>Primary hyperaldosteronism</strong> (Conn&rsquo;s syndrome) - <strong>Glucocorticoid remediable aldosteronism</strong> - <strong>Adrenal adenoma/hyperplasia</strong> - <strong>Salt loading</strong> or <strong>mineralocorticoid therapy</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal</strong></td>\n<td>May be seen in <strong>essential hypertension</strong>, normal physiology</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>High</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates <strong>renin stimulation</strong>, can be due to: - <strong>Renovascular hypertension</strong> - <strong>Renin-secreting tumor</strong> - <strong>Diuretic use</strong>, <strong>volume depletion</strong>, <strong>low sodium intake</strong> - <strong>Heart failure</strong>, <strong>cirrhosis</strong>, <strong>nephrotic syndrome</strong> (due to perceived low perfusion)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p data-start=\"2671\" data-end=\"2692\"><strong data-start=\"2675\" data-end=\"2692\">Clinical Uses</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"2693\" data-end=\"2919\">\n<li data-start=\"2693\" data-end=\"2766\">\n<p data-start=\"2695\" data-end=\"2766\"><strong data-start=\"2695\" data-end=\"2736\">Diagnosing primary hyperaldosteronism</strong> (low renin, high aldosterone)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2767\" data-end=\"2841\">\n<p data-start=\"2769\" data-end=\"2841\"><strong data-start=\"2769\" data-end=\"2810\">Identifying renovascular hypertension</strong> (high renin, high aldosterone)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2842\" data-end=\"2874\">\n<p data-start=\"2844\" data-end=\"2874\"><strong data-start=\"2844\" data-end=\"2874\">Assessing adrenal function</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2875\" data-end=\"2919\">\n<p data-start=\"2877\" data-end=\"2919\"><strong data-start=\"2877\" data-end=\"2919\">Evaluating drug effects on RAAS system</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
